/T (replacing lowercase 'i' with lowercase 'l' \(letter L\), or replacing 'rn' with 'm'. The resulting domain looks authentic to the human eye at a glance, especially in email clients, browser address bars, or mobile screens where font rendering compresses spacing. This makes homoglyph domains the most dangerous class for targeted spear-phishing, CEO fraud, and credential harvesting.)
